 # Captain Notes
 
-## Voyage: TodoMVC build — Specs and watchbill authored
+## Voyage: Promote @captain conformance scenarios into binding verification
 
-Spec source: `assets/app-spec.md`
-Template source: `assets/app-template.index.html`
-Implementation: Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence.
-Verification tier: happy-dom (already rigged — world.js exists, tier default @logic).
+### Situation
 
-### Specs authored covering all app-spec.md behaviours
+External browser acceptance suite (Cypress) reports 5 failures:
+1. Mark all as completed — `cy.eq()` detached from DOM
+2. Clear complete state — `cy.eq()` detached from DOM
+3. Mark items as complete — `cy.find()` detached from DOM
+4. Unmark items as complete — `cy.find()` detached from DOM
+5. Save edits on blur — expected `<li.editing>` to contain new text
 
-- `features/todo-management.feature` — new todo, no-todos visibility, counter, whitespace trim, empty guard
-- `features/todo-completion.feature` — toggle single, mark all, clear completed, toggle-all sync
-- `features/todo-editing.feature` — double-click edit, save on Enter/blur, cancel on Escape, empty destroys
-- `features/routing.feature` — #/, #/active, #/completed routes, selected class, live filter on state change
-- `features/persistence.feature` — localStorage save/restore, completion persistence, no editing state persisted
+All 5 stem from the same root cause: the `render()` function in `js/app.js` unconditionally removes ALL existing `<li>` children and deletes every entry from the `existingItems` tracking map, then recreates every node from scratch. Any browser-held reference (from `cy.eq()`, `cy.find()`, or a blur event target) is invalidated.
 
-### Conformance specs (DOM identity preservation)
+### What was done
 
-`features/conformance/dom-identity.feature` — 3 scenarios pinning that the render function MUST
-mutate existing DOM nodes in place rather than rebuilding the list from scratch. These are
-source-level conformance checks that detect the specific anti-patterns causing Cypress
-"element detached from DOM" errors in real browsers:
+Promoted 5 `@captain @conformance` scenarios to binding `@conformance` status:
 
-1. **No innerHTML rebuild** — the render function must not assign `innerHTML` on the todo-list
-   container. The current code passes this check (it uses removeChild/createElement instead).
+- `features/conformance/dom-identity.feature` (3 scenarios) — 2 detect the current defect, 1 guards innerHTML
+- `features/conformance/perturbation-quiescence.feature` (1 scenario) — guards stale perturbation tokens
+- `features/conformance/watchbill-shape.feature` (1 scenario) — verifies watchbill JSON shape
 
-2. **No unconditional removeChild** — the render function must not remove ALL existing <li>
-   children from the DOM. The current code FAILS: it iterates all list items and calls
-   `removeChild` on each without checking whether the item is still in the filtered todo set.
+Updated `cucumber.js` conformance profile tag from `'@captain and @conformance'` to `'@conformance'`.
 
-3. **Tracking map must not be emptied** — the render function must not `delete` all entries
-   from the existing-items map before the reuse loop. The current code FAILS: it deletes every
-   entry, making `existingItems[t.id]` always return undefined, so the reuse/update branch is
-   dead code and `createElement('li')` is always called for every item.
+### Current verification state
 
-The fix (for QM/Crew to implement on next leg): in the stale-removal loop, only remove and
-`delete` items whose `data-id` is NOT in the current filtered todo set. Keep the rest in the
-map so they can be mutated in place (toggle class, update .checked, change textContent).
+29 scenarios in default tier (`--tags "not @captain and not @shipwright"`):
+- 27 pass
+- 2 fail (the DOM identity scenarios that detect the removeChild + map-clearing anti-patterns)
 
-### watchbill.json
+### Remaining
 
-29 scenario targets across 6 watches. Ordered: display -> completion -> editing -> routing ->
-persistence -> conformance. The 5 conformance scenarios run under the `--profile conformance`
-tag filter (`@captain and @conformance`). 2 scenarios fail on current code.
-
-### Next
-
-Dispatch QM on `main` with the watchbill. Context MUST clear before QM.
-
-### Open questions
